=== task: multi medium
title: Safe pruning
prompt: A search rolls 3 dice, one at a time, looking for every roll whose total is exactly 10. Choose **every** check that can safely stop a partial roll early, without losing any answer.
* The total so far is already more than 10 :: Right. Every die adds at least 1, so the total can only grow.
* Even rolling 6 on every remaining die can't bring the total up to 10 :: Right. No completion can reach 10.
* The total so far plus 1 for every remaining die is more than 10 :: Right. Even the smallest possible rolls overshoot.
- The last die rolled was a 1 :: A 1 can still be part of a 10, like 1, 3, 6.
- The total so far is odd :: The remaining dice can make the total odd or even.
- The first die is a 6 :: 6, 1, 3 totals 10.
hint: A safe check proves that no way of finishing the roll can hit exactly 10.
hint: What are the smallest and the biggest totals the remaining dice can add?
right: Safe pruning only cuts branches that provably contain no answer: too big already, too big even with all 1s, or too small even with all 6s.
wrong: Prune only when every completion fails. The remaining dice add at least 1 and at most 6 each, so compare the total with those bounds; facts like the last die or the parity don't rule anything out.

