        results.append(path.upper())
```
hint: Letters have two options; other characters have one.
hint: Each option moves on to index i + 1, with the new string.
right: Each letter doubles the number of results, and the digit doesn't: 2 × 1 × 2 = 4 strings, lower case first at each letter.
wrong: Base case: when i reaches the end, record the path. If `s[i]` is a letter, recurse with its lower case and then its upper case added; otherwise recurse with the character as it is.
